[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387302544","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111435#issuecomment-3387302544","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111435","id":3387302544,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J5iKQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T19:56:40Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T19:56:40Z","body":"I'm not sure about this. I don't know if this is the only way to solve the enum issue, but having to declare each virtual method 3 times (`GDVIRTUAL*()` in the header, the new macros here in the cpp file and `GDVIRTUAL_BIND()` in `_bind_methods()`) is a lot of times","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387302544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387514039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111435#issuecomment-3387514039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111435","id":3387514039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J6Vy3","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T21:16:08Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T21:16:08Z","body":"Oh, I guess it is optional, though. I had initially thought this was changing the model so the virtual method _had_ to be split between header and source file, but that's not the case. So, I guess this would only be used when really needed. Increasing the size of `gdvirtual.gen.inc` so much for something that probably wouldn't be used that often isn't ideal, though","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387514039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387700906","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111435#issuecomment-3387700906","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111435","id":3387700906,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J7Daq","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-09T22:40:45Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T22:40:45Z","body":"Yeah, I'm not 100% happy with it either. There's honestly a LOT of bloat in that file, so maybe this idea could be paired with a broader trimming pass? Will play around with it this weekend","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3387700906/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3388657117","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111435#issuecomment-3388657117","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111435","id":3388657117,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7J-s3d","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T07:34:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T07:34:55Z","body":"Aside from the enum issue which I haven't looked into in-depth, I think the main issue with `GDVIRTUAL*` (with regard to #111218) is having to include a fairly heavy `gdvirtual.gen.inc` in headers. For example it's included in `core/os/main_loop.h` and `core/io/resource.h` so we can assume it's included pretty much everywhere.\r\n\r\nSo I could see value in splitting declaration from definition if we also split it into two separate headers (e.g. `gdvirtual_declare.gen.inc` and `gdvirtual_impl.gen.inc`), with the former being (I would expect) significantly smaller than the current header. That IMO could make it worth having to go through a 3-step registration instead of 2-step.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3388657117/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3401780781","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111435#issuecomment-3401780781","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111435","id":3401780781,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Kww4t","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T13:18:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T14:43:33Z","body":"As part of the new typing system, I'd like to eventually refactor the virtual function system such that it is as simple as a regular C++ virtual function table: Whether it would call an internal implementation, or one from GDExtension, or one from a script (if they'll still exist then) would all be decided by which pointer is stored in the active `GDType`.\r\nThis refactor would also require changing the interface of `GDVIRTUAL` (because the function pointer would be attached to the type instead of the object), and would also solve the problems addressed here.\r\n\r\nHowever, this might be quite far in the future still. But given that I think we'll simplify the whole system eventually anyway, I'm not sure if we want to introduce a \"secondary system\" (split declaration + definition) `GDVIRTUAL` before then.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3401780781/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402280850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111435#issuecomment-3402280850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111435","id":3402280850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Kyq-S","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T14:54:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T14:54:46Z","body":"Ohhh, constraining that sort of logic to `GDType` would be excellent! You could very easily abstract away the overwhelming majority of this logic to a single `void**` argument when the relevant metadata to unwrap it is already stored. That'd *also* have the ability to consolidate `MODBIND` and `EXBIND` too, centralizing the functionality even further\r\n\r\nWith that in mind, I'll say that this isn't something we need to worry about. It's very much addressing a symptom, rather than a cause. I'll shift priority to eliminating the need for forward-declare workarounds on some of our most expensive classes (`TypedArray` and `TypedDictionary` in particular, by revisiting #96741)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3402280850/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]